you wouldn't think it'd take very much  to convince someone to direct the latest  installment in the hugely successful  batman film franchise but as it turns  out there was one huge reason matt  reeves didn't want to take the job keep  watching to find out what it was  and  here we  go the latest reboot featuring dc comics  famed caped crusader the batman is  hitting theaters worldwide finally  completing a monumental task undertaken  by writer director matt reeves the  batman of course has undergone different  iterations during its arduous production  cycle which began with filmmaker zack  snyder's batman choice ben affleck not  only starring in the title role but also  writing and directing the film when  affleck left his batman project behind  over personal reasons the film's studio  warner brothers had to figure out who  could take charge of the project next  fostered by celebrated filmmaker j.j  abrams on the writer director's wb  series felicity matt reeves film  breakthrough came at the helm of the  abrams produced found footage monster  movie cloverfield the doors of  opportunity swung wide open for reeves  after the success of that film which  earned 172 million dollars at the  worldwide box office against a 25  million dollar budget this landed the  filmmaker such high-profile gigs as 20th  century films rise of the planet of the  ape sequels dawn of the planet of the  apes and war for the planet of the apes  in 2014 and 2017 respectively suddenly  reeves was calling his own shots as both  writer and director of the last two  films in the apes trilogy which was  clearly the right move for the studio to  make seeing how the entire trilogy is  widely considered one of the best in  modern cinema it also gave reeves the  kind of showbiz juice to make demands on  future projects that other filmmakers  might not get to make in a new interview  with the new york times reeves said he  was in post-production on war for the  planet of the apes when warner brothers  asked him to direct affleck's version of  the batman and while reeves told the  outlet that the iteration of the tale  was quote a totally valid and cool take  on the dark knight it just wasn't the  right story for him to direct he said i  just didn't know how i would direct that  oh take it easy sweetheart that's right  instead of following in the footsteps of  such revered batman directors tim burton  christopher nolan and snyder reeves put  the studio on ice declining to shoot the  script they'd sent him he recalled to  the times i don't think you're going to  want me because i wouldn't do this and  then they asked me what i would do i  said i'm in the middle of making this  apes movie so i can't really tell you  after finishing war for the planet of  the apes however reeves came back to  warner brothers with the one condition  he needed to direct the film he needed  to write his own original script the  writer director pitched his ideas for  the batman and began writing the  screenplay in 2017 after five years and  various pandemic induced production and  release delays the batman starring  robert pattinson as batman and zoe  kravitz as catwoman opened in theaters  in march of 2022 it's clear from the  interviews he's given that matt reeves  has the utmost respect for the character  and mythos of batman he didn't want to  just go in and make any old batman movie  he wanted to create a definitive dark  knight story for a new generation as he  went on to tell the times that involved  taking a novel approach to the caped  crusader i wanted to fight against any  sense that batman would remain static i  wanted the stakes of the story to  challenge him in a way that shook him to  his core he has to change to accomplish  that reeves had to go darker than any  live-action feature-length batman had  gone before as reeves told time magazine  i wanted to play on this idea that  batman is going to unleash on these guys  and there's a part of you that can't  wait to see it but reeves didn't want  the same old fight scenes in his film he  wanted to go bigger and darker as he  went on to explain you go to a batman  movie to see that moment and then you  see it's having a toxic effect it makes  you get a little unsettled  check out one of our newest videos right  here plus even more looper videos about  the batman are coming soon subscribe to  our youtube channel and hit the bell so  you don't miss a single one  [Music]
 

